{%- doc -%}
  Renders a 40px round thumbnail for a mobile drawer menu link (level-2 or level-3), when the
  linked collection has a `custom.menu_image` metafield. Metafield only, no featured_image
  fallback, so a plain collection/page link (or a placeholder "#" link) stays text-only - this
  is purely data-driven, independent of which desktop mega-menu panel style (tabbed, grid, or
  none) the top-level item happens to match, so it works the same for every drawer row.

  Matches the desktop grid mega menu's own thumbnail treatment (`.ft-grid__thumb`, see
  snippets/mega-menu-grid.liquid) so a row reads the same whether seen on desktop or in the
  drawer, except a drawer row without the metafield renders nothing at all here (the desktop
  grid always reserves an empty placeholder circle; the drawer's plain text rows should not
  gain one).

  @param {object} link - The drawer link (childlink or grandchildlink) to check for a menu image.

  @example
  {% render 'menu-drawer-thumb', link: childlink %}
{%- enddoc -%}

{% liquid
  assign menu_image = link.object.metafields.custom.menu_image.value
%}
{% if menu_image %}
  <span class="menu-drawer__thumb">
    {{
      menu_image
      | image_url: width: 80
      | image_tag:
        loading: 'lazy',
        widths: '40, 80',
        sizes: '40px',
        class: 'menu-drawer__thumb-img',
        alt: link.title
    }}
  </span>
{% endif %}
